    {
      "title": "113 arrested over violence during drivers' protest in Bhubaneswar: Police",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/113-arrested-over-violence-during-drivers-protest-in-bhubaneswar-police-126082000297_1.html",
      "description": "Odisha Police have so far arrested 113 people for their alleged involvement in the violence during a protest of app-based cab and auto-rickshaw drivers and motorcycle riders in Bhubaneswar, officials said on Thursday.\nWhile 113 people have been arrested and forwarded to the court, another 60 detained people have been released on bond of good behaviour, a police officer of the Bhubaneswar-Cuttack Police Commissionerate said.\nThe police have also seized 354 vehicles for violating norms, he said.\nSo far, seven FIRs have been registered against the protesters at Kharvel Nagar police station here in this connection with the violence.\n\"Anyone taking law into their hands will be dealt with strictly as per law,\" he added.\nDrivers and riders registered with various online ride-hailing platforms began a cease-work on August 17, pressing for the fulfilment of their seven-point charter of demands, including a fare hike, reduction in application fees, social security and other benefits.\nHundr",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-20T05:55:38"
    }
  ]
